      "functional_impact_measured": "EGF-induced phosphorylation at Tyr1086 and Tyr978 was preserved at levels comparable to wild-type; downstream ERK levels and ERK phosphorylation upon EGF activation were unaltered (L6, A549 cells).",
      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "The landmarks fix the signal peptide at residues 1\u201324 (last residue A) and the mature N-terminus at residue 25 (L); insert_after_residue=24 places the tag in the extracellular domain, 621 residues from the TM boundary, with no proximity concern. L6 (same construct as L2/L3) confirms EGF-induced phosphorylation and ERK signalling are intact, meeting the surface_and_function threshold. L1 independently validates the identical junction via CRISPR knock-in of a FAP tag at the endogenous locus, confirming the position is tolerant of insertions of varying size. Python verified residue_before=A and residue_after=L from the canonical sequence. Flag-EGFR and Flag-EGFR-HaloTag constructs were transfected into A549 cells; the Flag tag was placed on the N-terminus of the ECD, explicitly downstream of the signal peptide and upstream of the mature EGFR sequence. Surface display was confirmed by anti-Flag flow cytometry (L3). A parallel CRISPR knock-in of a FAP tag at the identical junction in the endogenous locus was also reported (L1).",
      "sources": [
        {
          "source_id": "DOI:10.1101/2024.12.21.629933",
          "citation": "DOI 10.1101/2024.12.21.629933",
          "claim": "In order to validate that the tagged EGFR constructs functioned properly upon EGF ligand activation, we incubated the engineered cells with EGF and observed significant activation of wellknown and functional phosphorylation sites on EGFR, Tyr1086 and Tyr978, 27 at comparable levels to the wild-type cells ( Figure 1C ).We also confirmed that the cell engineering did not significantly alter the patterns of downstream ERK levels or ERK phosphorylation upon EGF activation."
        }
